    VALUES (subj, tid, 'THEORY', 'A circuit with ideal elements is shown. Which one of the following options correctly identifies all the linear elements in the circuit?', 'A circuit with ideal elements is shown.

![Figure](fig:q-gate2026-23)

Which one of the following options correctly identifies all the linear elements in the circuit?
', '**Idea used:** linear ⇔ obeys superposition (additivity + homogeneity) (see *Kinds of circuit elements*).

- **R:** $v = Ri$, a straight line through the origin ⇒ linear.
- **L:** $v = L\,di/dt$. Differentiation is a linear operation (the derivative of a sum is the sum of derivatives, and of $k\,i$ is $k\,di/dt$) ⇒ linear.
- **C:** $i = C\,dv/dt$ ⇒ linear for the same reason.
- **D (diode):** conducts one way only; its v–i curve is not a straight line ⇒ **non-linear**.
- **$V_{DC}$:** an independent source is the input (excitation) of the circuit, not one of its linear elements; its v–i graph $v = V_{DC}$ does not pass through the origin.

So the linear elements are R, L and C.

**Answer: (B) R, L, and C only.**
', 'READY', 'MCQ', NULL, NULL, 1, 'UNVERIFIED', 'gate-2026-23', 'PYQ') RETURNING id INTO qid;
